Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||06-12-2001||10:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>My question is? no flaming intended, are you gonna drive it or waste another fiero(s)?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Galen , Please stop worrying about wasting a Fiero.<P>You say no flaming intended, your putting down someone's choice to keep their Feiro with low mileage.<P>Owning a Fiero is a joy,  Speaking for myself, those that have low mileage cars do not wish to be put down for their choice.<P>Period.  This is a simple and and fair request. <P>It's like giving someone grief for painting a Fiero a non stock color.<P>Or shaming someone for mounting custom wheels on a Fiero.<P>As silly as those two examples look, so does giving someone grief for low mileage.<P>Since you know this is a topic that upsets, at least me, please stop.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GT||06-12-2001||10:07 PM||||I would much rather know that somebody has a low mileage fiero(above) that they dont drive than to have the above fiero turned to a kitcar.  Thats my opinion.  Good find to you on the 88GT!  Hope you enjoy it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||06-12-2001||10:34 PM||||Cool Blue, I May have seemed to put you down a bit after the Daytona show. I just don't have the ability not to drive my 87 Blue GT. I make up places to go just so I can drive it.<P> I understand and appreciate your point of view and the fact I can actually see a low mileage Blue 87. <P>I'll be at Daytona 2002 and will get to see your fine car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and shake your hand!<BR>Coy ||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||06-12-2001||10:36 PM||||You gotta wonder though, how badly did this guy in Alaska lose his ass? There ain't no way to make money on keeping a no mileage car around. If that's what you wanna do, more power to ya, but I'm with Galen on this one. Kind of a waste. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||06-12-2001||11:25 PM||||Hard for me to decide on this one.  You have to appreciate how awesome such low mileage cars are.  That's incredible!  But for me, It'd kill me to have that car and not be able to drive it.  I had an original, numbers matching 72 Trans Am.  It wasn't low mileage, but I felt obligated to the car's history to keep it all original.  To me, this hampered my fun somewhat.  <P>Ideally, I'd want the low mileage original to keep and show, and another "regular" one that I can go out and blast around in all time.  I definately see both sides here.||||reg||6
Z||000009||XDrewX||06-12-2001||11:54 PM||||I am playing both sides of the fence<P>one one hand i have my bone stock 87 gt, which i am going to keep that way, because it is awesome.<P>on the other hand i have my 86 gt which will somday be getting a lamborghini kit.<P>since i could walk, i have always wanted a lamborghini, and buying a body kit and some authentic pieces to complete it, is the closest i will ever come to really owning one.  <P>So in saying all of that i guess i can see both points of view. <BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||CoolBlue87GT||06-13-2001||12:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RobMich:<BR><B>This is the one I had been looking for for years.... I am in Fiero Heaven!!!!<BR>Rob</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Can't wait to see the pic's ! Happy for you.<P><BR>Ref: the short talk about mileage, glad both sides can be seen.<P>Keeping low miles is a choice - not a wrong one, not a right one.  -  just a choice<P>That all.  As long as people can agree on that, then I'm happy.||||reg||1
