Z||000013||Fformula88||06-13-2001||08:04 AM||||Congrats on the awesome find.  I must agree that the cars should be driven, but don't look at a car being kept with low milage as "wasting" a car.  Think of it as saving it for later.  It might be the last Fiero on the road in the future!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||RRobinson||06-13-2001||12:38 PM||||The way I see this low milage thing is that my hobbies are driving AND preserving Fieros for the future. In 2040, it will sure be neat to have an all original unrestored 88 GT to show people. Look at it this way- I'm sure glad no one "drove" all the '67 Corvette convertibles or Shelby Cobras to death.<P>I plan on driving the new GT 3 or 4 times a year, otherwise, it sits tucked away in my garage with the rest of 'em.<P>Long live the low milage fieros!<P>Ryan<BR>88 GT 5.5K miles<BR>88 GT 40K<BR>87 GT 18K<BR>87 GT 56K<BR>87 SE V6 111K ...This one's for drivin'<BR>86 GT 42K||||reg||1
