Z||000018||elfiero||06-13-2001||03:54 PM||||I guess I don't really much care if people<BR>drive them or not.The only thing I've wondered about is,it was hard enough to keep<BR>pre-'70 cars "mint" and if not for the interest in muscle cars(the reproduction of<BR>discontinued parts)there would'nt be any GTO,<BR>mustangs,ect.The point I'm making is this  these mid-80's cars are going<BR>to shrevel up and crumble due to less than<BR>perfect humidity,UV rays,and just think of<BR>the ability to maintain electrical connection<BR>integrety.contrary to what most people think<BR>these and all 70's&up cars are engineered to<BR>last about 15 years max!Look at your wiring<BR>looms and various other plastic parts on your<BR>beloved little car if you don't belive me.So,<BR>if you keep it as a musiem peice,thats fine<BR>but driving it "once in a while" is the worst<BR>thing you could do to it!keep it in doors <BR>and in a heated&air conditioned area and don't open the doors(wears out parts)then you<BR>will have a true collectors peice!.this is<BR>not meant as a put down,but as far as I'm<BR>concerned,cars are a sh*tty investment so I<BR>am gonna drive the wheels off my totally<BR>modified,custom painted 87GT b-4 all the <BR>parts are gone.these are my veiws and not<BR>intended to flame!<p>[This message has been edited by elfiero (edited 06-13-2001).]||||reg||6
