Z||000020||84Bill||06-13-2001||07:42 PM||||I have an Indy I'm going to restore FULLY. I'm going to replace every component I can with new parts even if they work. Call me crazy but that the way I want to do it. I'm not going to roll back the 121,000 on the odometer or anything like that. I want an Indy Fiero that is as new and as stock as I can possibly make it. I don't care how long it takes me, I'm in no hurry. It's not going to be a daily driver when it's done but I will definatly drive it to shows (but not to far). It may be ready for Carlisle 2003 or 4 or what ever. Watch out CoolBlue87GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I want that Stock class trophy.||||reg||14
Z||000021||CoolBlue87GT||06-13-2001||10:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84Bill:<BR><B>I have an Indy ...It may be ready for Carlisle 2003 or 4 or what ever. Watch out CoolBlue87GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I want that Stock class trophy.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>:&gt; )  Looking forward to seeing the Indy when you finish it !! (&lt;:<P>As for the trophy, I wasn't expecting to get it this time, I saw a few that I though would win. (did have my fingers crossed though)<P>Mostly enjoy the friendships made & all the different Fiero's at the shows. Carlise was my first show out of state. Daytona was my first out of town show.<P>Enough about me, don't want to steal his thunder, This newly found 88 should be awesome.||||reg||1
Z||000022||84Bill||06-13-2001||11:15 PM||||Congratulations Rob! nice find, I hope you can get us some pictures soon. I'm glad you car has a good home and someone that appriciates what they have.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW You definatly deserved that trophy Dave  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">It's the nicest machine I have ever laid eyes on. Keep in mind nw I have not see Rob's car yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||Galen||06-14-2001||09:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>galen are you going to keep risking your fiero and exposing it to the dangers of the road?when cars can hit it or scratch the finish, driving it in the harmfull sunshine<BR>or worse even in rain or hail ?<BR>the only way to drive a fiero is late at night after all others are in bed and only for short trips in dry condisions.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're a weird lil man. I've always thought that. but as for me 'risking' my 88? my rare lotus suspensioned 88, one simple word answers that.. Yes I am. Why not? they were made to be driven and enjoyed. Not to be looked at and enjoyed. Thats what concept cars are for. Not production vehicles.<P>Rob, nice car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> congrats ||||reg||1
Z||000024||CoolBlue87GT||06-14-2001||11:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84Bill:<BR><B>BTW You definatly deserved that trophy Dave   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">It's the nicest machine I have ever laid eyes on. Keep in mind nw I have not see Rob's car yet   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks 84Bill.  I like this new button I found, it allow you to ignore those that<BR>are pests.<P>I'm glad to see there aren't any posts between yours and mine.  <P>It works good !   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
